course: dictionary
lesson: 15282
title: Simultaneously means at the same time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Simultaneously is a formal word that means at exactly the same time. Simpler words for it are «at the same time» and «at once». «The two taps filled the bath simultaneously» means both taps were running together.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. Two things happen together, not one after the other. «The bell rang and the doors opened simultaneously.» Ask yourself: did both things start and finish at the same moment? If yes, simultaneously fits.
explain: In maths, simultaneously means working on things together. «Solve these two equations simultaneously» means find the numbers that make both equations true at the same time, not solve one and forget the other.
fact: Simultaneously means at exactly the same time.
fact: Simpler words with the same meaning are «at the same time» and «at once».
fact: Simultaneously is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens, like «quickly» or «slowly».
fact: The adjective is «simultaneous», as in «simultaneous events», which happen at the same time.
fact: In maths, «solve simultaneously» means find values that make two or more equations true together.
exercise: «The two trains left the station simultaneously.» What does simultaneously mean? | Never at all | One after the other | Very slowly | *At exactly the same time
exercise: Which words could replace simultaneously in «The lights and the music started simultaneously»? | at home | *at the same time | at the bottom | at last
exercise: Maths: «Solve the two equations simultaneously» means | add up all the numbers | solve the first one, then forget the second | draw a graph of the first one only | *find the numbers that make both equations true together
test: «Two taps filled the tank simultaneously.» What is true? | The tank was already full | The taps took turns, one after the other | Only one tap was switched on | *Both taps were running at the same time
test: Which word is the adjective from simultaneously? | simultaneously | simulate | simultaneity | *simultaneous
exam: Which sentence uses simultaneously correctly? | I ate my breakfast simultaneously before it was morning. | *The two bells rang simultaneously at noon. | The dog barked simultaneously, one bark after the other. | Simultaneously is a name for a very long day.
